## Claim
Text: "The U.S. surgeon general and the Centers for Disease Control both previously said that ‘masks are not effective in preventing [the] general public from catching coronavirus.’"
Claim author: Yinon Weiss
Claim date: October 29, 2020
Claim origin: https://thefederalist.com/2020/10/29/these-12-graphs-show-mask-mandates-do-nothing-to-stop-covid/

## Initial Q&A
### Did the U.S. Surgeon General make a public statement prior to October 29, 2020, that said masks are not effective for the general public in preventing coronavirus infection?
Answer: Yes, the U.S. Surgeon General did make such a public statement. In a tweet, Dr. Jerome Adams stated that "face masks are not effective in preventing spread of COVID-19," urging the public to stop buying them to preserve supply for healthcare workers.

Source URL: https://www.kcrg.com/content/news/US-Surgeon-General-face-masks-are-not-effective-in-preventing-spread-of-COVID-19-568391361.html

### Did the Centers for Disease Control and Prevention (CDC) publish official guidance prior to October 29, 2020, that stated masks are not effective for the general public in preventing coronavirus infection?
Answer: No, the CDC did not publish official guidance stating masks are ineffective for the general public; rather, its guidance evolved as understanding of the virus changed. According to the source, on April 3, 2020, the CDC changed its recommendation to advise that all Americans wear non-medical masks, indicating a shift from earlier, more limited guidance.

Source URL: https://time.com/5774521/coronavirus-face-mask-prevention/

### What were the exact dates on which the U.S. Surgeon General and the CDC made the statements regarding masks and coronavirus effectiveness cited in this claim?
Answer: The U.S. Surgeon General made the statement on March 8, as he said in an interview with "Face the Nation" that "masks do not work for the general public and preventing them from getting coronavirus." The search result does not provide a specific date for a corresponding statement from the CDC.

Source URL: https://www.cbsnews.com/news/coronavirus-surgeon-general-jerome-adams-wearing-masks-face-the-nation/

